  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Established in 1990, the Auckland Institute of Studies (AIS) is the largest independent tertiary education provider in Auckland. You will find a nurturing and friendly environment that balances rigorous academic programmes with personalised attention through small class sizes. AIS is particularly well-regarded for its practical approach to learning, focusing on high-demand sectors like Business Administration, Information Technology, and Hospitality Management.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">At AIS, you will experience a truly multicultural environment, with students representing various countries from across the globe. The institute prioritises your wellbeing through dedicated student support managers who assist with non-academic issues and pastoral care. You can participate in study skills workshops, cultural sensitivity initiatives, and social events that help you build lifelong international networks.</span></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">AIS offers safe and inclusive student accommodation facilities. You can choose from on-campus residences that provide a convenient and positive living environment, or seek assistance for finding budget-friendly options off-campus. The student support team is available to help you navigate your housing needs to ensure you have a comfortable stay while studying in Auckland.</span><br>&nbsp;</p><p>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, visit the Edvoy <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/student/stays\">Stays</a> feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<h3><strong>1. Library</strong></h3><p>The AIS Library provides you with essential academic resources, including physical books and digital learning environments. It serves as a quiet study space where you can access the research tools necessary for your diploma, undergraduate, or postgraduate studies.</p><h3><strong>2. Sports</strong></h3><p>You will have access to recreational opportunities near the campuses, such as the Chamberlain Park Golf Course, which is adjacent to the St Helens campus. The university environment encourages an active lifestyle to support your physical and mental health.</p><h3><strong>3. Laboratories</strong></h3><p>AIS features specialised laboratories designed for hands-on training, particularly for students in the Information Technology and Hospitality programmes. These include modern computer labs and practical training facilities that simulate real-world work environments.</p><h3><strong>4. Cafeteria</strong></h3><p>Dining options are available on campus, offering you a place to relax and socialise with classmates between lectures. You can find fresh food and beverages to keep you fueled throughout your study day.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<h3><strong>St Helens Campus</strong></h3><p>Located in Mt Albert, this campus is set in spacious, park-like grounds next to the Chamberlain Park Golf Course. It is well-connected to the city via the Baldwin Avenue train station and frequent bus services. This campus serves as the primary hub for many degree programmes and student support services.</p><h3><strong>Asquith Campus</strong></h3><p>Situated just a five-minute walk from the St Helens campus, the Asquith Campus is close to the St Lukes shopping centre. It offers excellent transport links to the city and western suburbs, making it a convenient location for your studies.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
